        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0792" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg696"/>

                <head>No. 315.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokei,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1879-10-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 10, 1879</date>. (Received
                        November 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 988.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 125, dated September
                    26, 1874, it gives me pleasure to say that by the amended code of this
                    government trial by torture is altogether abrogated in the Japanese Empire.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose herewith the notification on this subject of his
                    excellency Sanjo Saneyoshi, the prime minister of His Majesty, as published in
                    the Japan Daily Mail of this date.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d344-a1.xml" xpointer="d344-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
